  "nativeName": "பாடல் பெற்ற தலங்கள்",
  "theme": "The 275 Shiva temples praised in the Tevaram hymns of the Nayanar saints",
  "region": "Tamil Nadu, Puducherry, Andhra Pradesh, Kerala, Karnataka, Sri Lanka & North India",
  "description": "The Paadal Petra Sthalams are the Shiva temples sung in the Tevaram, the seventh- and eighth-century Tamil hymns of the three great Nayanar saints — Tirugnana Sambandar, Tirunavukkarasar (Appar) and Sundarar. To visit them is to follow the saints' own footsteps across the Tamil country. Tradition gathers them region by region: the great belt of the Chola country along the Kaveri, north bank and south bank; the Pandya country around Madurai; Nadu Nadu between the Pennai and the Kollidam; Kongu Nadu in the west; Thondai Nadu around Kanchipuram; and a few beyond — one in Kerala, one at Gokarna on the Konkan, two in Sri Lanka, and a handful in the north from Srisailam to Kailash. They are the Shaiva counterpart of the Vaishnava Divya Desams, and the living map of Tamil devotion to Shiva. Gathered here region by region, each region with its own route map.",
